### What version of Codex CLI is running?

codex-cli 0.160.0 (npm `@openai/codex@0.160.0`, win32-x64). Also reproduced on codex-cli 0.159.2, the CLI bundled with the Codex desktop app.

### What subscription do you have?

ChatGPT Pro 500

### Which model were you using?

gpt-6-astra (the default in config.toml), with `-c model_reasoning_effort="low"`

### What platform is your computer?

Microsoft Windows NT 10.0.26200.0 x64 (Windows 11 Pro, build 26200.9457)

### What terminal emulator and version are you using (if applicable)?

None: `codex exec --json` runs under a Node.js supervisor with piped stdin/stdout/stderr and no console. Shell commands run in Windows PowerShell 5.1.26100.9444.

### Codex doctor report

```json
Not included, to keep local configuration private. Relevant here: 7 MCP servers are configured (see the steps below), and the shell is Windows PowerShell 5.1.
```

### What issue are you seeing?

`codex exec` prints `turn.completed`, but `codex.exe` does not exit while a process that the agent started during the turn is still running. The trigger is a process started with `Start-Process ... -RedirectStandardOutput <file> -RedirectStandardError <file>`. While it waits:

- `codex.exe` sits idle;
- its only child is `conhost.exe`;
- it exits within a fraction of a second after that detached process exits.

If the detached process is a long-running server, `codex exec` never exits.

How we hit it: our supervisor waits for `codex exec` to exit before it starts the next job. One unattended run restarted a local dev server this way. `codex exec` then stayed alive for about 11 minutes after `turn.completed`, blocking the queue, until we killed it.

The same command without `-RedirectStandardOutput/-RedirectStandardError` does not keep `codex exec` alive. Reproduced on 0.160.0 and 0.159.2.

### What steps can reproduce the bug?

1. Start `codex exec` from any non-interactive parent. We used Node `child_process.spawn` with `stdio: ['pipe','pipe','pipe']`, wrote the prompt to stdin and closed it:

   ```
   codex exec --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox --skip-git-repo-check --json --cd <empty dir> -c model_reasoning_effort="low" -
   ```

2. Use this prompt:

   ```
   This is an automated test of your shell tool.
   Use your shell tool exactly once to run the following PowerShell command, unchanged, in the current working directory.
   Do not run any other command, do not read or write any other file, and do not explain anything.
   When the command has returned, reply with exactly: DONE

   $p = Start-Process -FilePath 'powershell.exe' -ArgumentList '-NoProfile','-Command','Start-Sleep -Seconds 90' -WindowStyle Hidden -RedirectStandardOutput 'child.out.log' -RedirectStandardError 'child.err.log' -PassThru; Set-Content -LiteralPath 'child.pid' -Value $p.Id -NoNewline; "started $($p.Id)"
   ```

3. After `turn.completed`, `codex.exe` stays alive until the detached `Start-Sleep -Seconds 90` process exits.
4. Control: the same prompt with `-RedirectStandardOutput 'child.out.log' -RedirectStandardError 'child.err.log'` removed. `codex.exe` then exits a few seconds after `turn.completed`.

Results, one run per variant and version. Times are seconds since `codex exec` started.

| | 0.160.0 control | 0.160.0 redirect | 0.159.2 control | 0.159.2 redirect |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| shell call started → returned | 8.4 → 8.5 | 9.9 → 10.1 | 10.7 → 10.8 | 18.3 → 18.5 |
| `turn.completed` | 11.1 | 12.4 | 14.8 | 26.5 |
| `codex.exe` exited (exit code 0) | 14.9 | 100.0 | 18.3 | 108.5 |
| detached process first seen gone (polled every 0.5 s) | 98.6 | 100.5 | 101.1 | 109.0 |
| **`codex.exe` exit after `turn.completed`** | **3.8 s** | **87.6 s** | **3.5 s** | **82.0 s** |

The shell call starts the detached process and returns in under 0.2 s in every run, and the turn completes normally. In the control runs `codex.exe` exits while the detached process keeps running for more than 80 s. In the redirect runs `codex.exe` exits 90.2 s after the detached process was created, which is when its `Start-Sleep -Seconds 90` ends.

Ten seconds after `turn.completed` in both redirect runs, `codex.exe` was idle: 12 threads, 352 to 421 handles, under 1 s of CPU time in total, and no child process except `conhost.exe`.

All runs had the same 7 MCP servers configured. Disabling them with `-c mcp_servers.<name>.enabled=false` failed on this setup, so they ran as configured. The control runs exit promptly with them, so they are not what keeps the process alive.

<details>
<summary>The harness we used for these timings (Node.js, about 350 lines). It only spawns <code>codex exec</code>, polls the detached PID, takes process snapshots and records timings.</summary>

```js
// codex-exec-hang-repro.mjs - minimal local reproduction for a `codex exec` exit problem on Windows.
//
// Question: does `codex exec` keep running after it has printed `turn.completed` when, during the turn, a shell
// command started a detached process with `Start-Process ... -RedirectStandardOutput/-RedirectStandardError`?
// With redirection, Windows PowerShell starts the process through CreateProcess with handle inheritance, so the
// detached process can inherit the shell tool's stdout/stderr pipe handles. The control variant starts the same
// detached process without redirection (ShellExecute, no handle inheritance).
//
// Each variant is one short `codex exec` turn: one shell command, then the reply "DONE". The detached process is
// `powershell.exe -NoProfile -Command Start-Sleep -Seconds <child-seconds>`, so it ends by itself.
// Measured per variant: when `turn.completed` arrives, when codex.exe exits, when the detached process exits.
// A watchdog kills codex.exe (taskkill /T /F) only if it is still running <grace-seconds> after `turn.completed`
// (or <hard-cap-seconds> after its start without a `turn.completed`). A detached process still alive at the end is
// stopped after its identity is checked.
//
// Usage (Windows):
//   node codex-exec-hang-repro.mjs --out <results dir> [--codex <codex.exe>] [--variants control,redirect]
//     [--child-seconds 90] [--grace-seconds 150] [--hard-cap-seconds 420] [--effort low] [--mcp off|as-configured]
//     [--work-root <dir>]
// Writes <out>/harness.log while it runs and <out>/results.json (with "done": true) at the end.

import { spawn, spawnSync } from 'node:child_process';
import { appendFileSync, existsSync, mkdirSync, readFileSync, readdirSync, statSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';
import { join, resolve } from 'node:path';
import os from 'node:os';

const isWin = process.platform === 'win32';
const sleep = (ms) => new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, ms));
const iso = (ms = Date.now()) => new Date(ms).toISOString();

const MINIMAL_ENV = isWin
  ? ['PATH', 'Path', 'PATHEXT', 'SystemRoot', 'windir', 'ComSpec', 'SystemDrive', 'TEMP', 'TMP', 'USERPROFILE', 'HOMEDRIVE', 'HOMEPATH', 'APPDATA', 'LOCALAPPDATA', 'ProgramData', 'ProgramFiles', 'ProgramFiles(x86)', 'ProgramW6432', 'CommonProgramFiles', 'CommonProgramFiles(x86)', 'PUBLIC', 'ALLUSERSPROFILE', 'USERNAME', 'USERDOMAIN', 'COMPUTERNAME', 'NUMBER_OF_PROCESSORS', 'PROCESSOR_ARCHITECTURE', 'OS', 'LANG', 'LC_ALL', 'TZ', 'HTTP_PROXY', 'HTTPS_PROXY', 'NO_PROXY', 'http_proxy', 'https_proxy', 'no_proxy']
  : ['PATH', 'HOME', 'USER', 'LOGNAME', 'SHELL', 'TMPDIR', 'LANG', 'LC_ALL', 'TERM', 'TZ', 'HTTP_PROXY', 'HTTPS_PROXY', 'NO_PROXY', 'http_proxy', 'https_proxy', 'no_proxy'];

function parseArgs(argv) {
  const opts = { out: null, codex: null, variants: ['control', 'redirect'], childSeconds: 90, graceSeconds: 150, hardCapSeconds: 420, effort: 'low', mcp: 'off', workRoot: null };
  for (let i = 0; i < argv.length; i += 1) {
    const flag = argv[i];
    const value = argv[i + 1];
    const need = () => { if (value === undefined || value.startsWith('--')) throw new Error(`${flag} needs a value`); i += 1; return value; };
    if (flag === '--out') opts.out = need();
    else if (flag === '--codex') opts.codex = need();
    else if (flag === '--variants') opts.variants = need().split(',').map((s) => s.trim()).filter(Boolean);
    else if (flag === '--child-seconds') opts.childSeconds = Number(need());
    else if (flag === '--grace-seconds') opts.graceSeconds = Number(need());
    else if (flag === '--hard-cap-seconds') opts.hardCapSeconds = Number(need());
    else if (flag === '--effort') opts.effort = need();
    else if (flag === '--mcp') opts.mcp = need();
    else if (flag === '--work-root') opts.workRoot = need();
    else throw new Error(`unknown argument ${flag}`);
  }
  if (!opts.out) throw new Error('--out <results dir> is required');
  for (const v of opts.variants) if (v !== 'control' && v !== 'redirect') throw new Error(`unknown variant ${v} (known: control, redirect)`);
  for (const [k, v] of Object.entries({ childSeconds: opts.childSeconds, graceSeconds: opts.graceSeconds, hardCapSeconds: opts.hardCapSeconds })) if (!Number.isFinite(v) || v <= 0) throw new Error(`${k} must be a positive number`);
  if (!['minimal', 'low', 'medium', 'high', 'xhigh'].includes(opts.effort)) throw new Error('--effort must be minimal, low, medium, high or xhigh');
  if (opts.mcp !== 'off' && opts.mcp !== 'as-configured') throw new Error('--mcp must be off or as-configured');
  return opts;
}

/** The newest codex.exe the Codex desktop app installed (newer of birth and modification time). */
function newestCodex() {
  const root = join(process.env.LOCALAPPDATA || '', 'OpenAI', 'Codex', 'bin');
  if (!existsSync(root)) return null;
  let best = null;
  for (const name of readdirSync(root)) {
    const exe = join(root, name, 'codex.exe');
    if (!existsSync(exe)) continue;
    const st = statSync(exe);
    const t = Math.max(st.birthtimeMs || 0, st.mtimeMs || 0);
    if (!best || t > best.t) best = { exe, t };
  }
  return best ? best.exe : null;
}

function minimalEnv() {
  const out = {};
  for (const key of MINIMAL_ENV) if (process.env[key] !== undefined) out[key] = process.env[key];
  return out;
}

/** Run a PowerShell script (encoded, so no quoting problems) and return its stdout, or null. */
function psRun(script, timeoutMs = 30_000) {
  if (!isWin) return null;
  const encoded = Buffer.from(script, 'utf16le').toString('base64');
  const r = spawnSync('powershell.exe', ['-NoProfile', '-NonInteractive', '-EncodedCommand', encoded], { encoding: 'utf8', windowsHide: true, timeout: timeoutMs });
  return { status: r.status, stdout: (r.stdout || '').trim(), stderr: (r.stderr || '').trim().slice(0, 2000) };
}
function psJson(script) {
  const r = psRun(script);
  if (!r) return null;
  try { return JSON.parse(r.stdout || 'null'); } catch { return { unparsed_stdout: r.stdout.slice(0, 2000), stderr: r.stderr }; }
}

function procInfo(pid) {
  if (!pid) return null;
  if (!isWin) {
    const r = spawnSync('ps', ['-o', 'pid=,ppid=,nlwp=,etimes=,args=', '-p', String(pid)], { encoding: 'utf8' });
    return r.stdout.trim() || null;
  }
  return psJson(`$p = Get-CimInstance Win32_Process -Filter "ProcessId=${Number(pid)}"
if ($p) { $c = [string]$p.CommandLine
  [pscustomobject]@{ pid = $p.ProcessId; ppid = $p.ParentProcessId; name = $p.Name; threads = $p.ThreadCount; handles = $p.HandleCount; working_set = $p.WorkingSetSize
    kernel_ms = [math]::Round($p.KernelModeTime / 10000); user_ms = [math]::Round($p.UserModeTime / 10000); created = $p.CreationDate.ToUniversalTime().ToString('o')
    command_line = $c.Substring(0, [math]::Min(300, $c.Length)) } | ConvertTo-Json -Compress } else { 'null' }`);
}
function childrenOf(pid) {
  if (!pid) return null;
  if (!isWin) {
    const r = spawnSync('ps', ['-o', 'pid=,args=', '--ppid', String(pid)], { encoding: 'utf8' });
    return r.stdout.trim() || [];
  }
  // Windows PowerShell 5.1: ConvertTo-Json has no -AsArray, so an empty or single result is handled explicitly.
  return psJson(`$list = @(Get-CimInstance Win32_Process -Filter "ParentProcessId=${Number(pid)}" | ForEach-Object { $c = [string]$_.CommandLine
  [pscustomobject]@{ pid = $_.ProcessId; name = $_.Name; created = $_.CreationDate.ToUniversalTime().ToString('o'); command_line = $c.Substring(0, [math]::Min(200, $c.Length)) } })
if ($list.Count -eq 0) { '[]' } else { ConvertTo-Json -InputObject $list -Compress }`);
}

function alive(pid) {
  if (!pid) return false;
  try { process.kill(pid, 0); return true; } catch (error) { return error.code === 'EPERM'; }
}

function killTree(pid) {
  if (!pid) return null;
  if (isWin) { const r = spawnSync('taskkill', ['/T', '/F', '/PID', String(pid)], { encoding: 'utf8', windowsHide: true, timeout: 15_000 }); return { status: r.status, stdout: (r.stdout || '').trim(), stderr: (r.stderr || '').trim() }; }
  try { process.kill(pid, 'SIGKILL'); return { status: 0 }; } catch (error) { return { status: 1, error: String(error) }; }
}

/** Stop the detached sleeper only if it still is the process this harness asked for (name and command line checked). */
function stopSleeper(pid, childSeconds) {
  if (!alive(pid)) return { stopped: false, reason: 'not running' };
  if (isWin) {
    const r = psRun(`$p = Get-CimInstance Win32_Process -Filter "ProcessId=${Number(pid)}"
if ($p -and $p.Name -eq 'powershell.exe' -and ([string]$p.CommandLine) -like '*Start-Sleep -Seconds ${Number(childSeconds)}*') { Stop-Process -Id ${Number(pid)} -Force; 'stopped' } else { 'identity mismatch: not stopped' }`);
    return { stopped: r?.stdout === 'stopped', reason: r?.stdout ?? 'no answer' };
  }
  try { process.kill(pid, 'SIGKILL'); return { stopped: true, reason: 'stopped' }; } catch (error) { return { stopped: false, reason: String(error) }; }
}

function commandFor(variant, childSeconds) {
  const start = `$p = Start-Process -FilePath 'powershell.exe' -ArgumentList '-NoProfile','-Command','Start-Sleep -Seconds ${childSeconds}' -WindowStyle Hidden`;
  const redirect = variant === 'redirect' ? ` -RedirectStandardOutput 'child.out.log' -RedirectStandardError 'child.err.log'` : '';
  return `${start}${redirect} -PassThru; Set-Content -LiteralPath 'child.pid' -Value $p.Id -NoNewline; "started $($p.Id)"`;
}

function promptFor(command) {
  return [
    'This is an automated test of your shell tool.',
    'Use your shell tool exactly once to run the following PowerShell command, unchanged, in the current working directory.',
    'Do not run any other command, do not read or write any other file, and do not explain anything.',
    'When the command has returned, reply with exactly: DONE',
    '',
    command,
    '',
  ].join('\n');
}

/** Did the shell tool call return while the detached process was still running, or only once it had exited? */
function toolCallVerdictOf(r) {
  const done = r.items.find((i) => i.type === 'item.completed' && i.command);
  if (!done) return 'no_command_completed';
  if (r.sleeper_pid === null) return 'detached_process_not_started';
  if (r.sleeper_exit_ms !== null && done.at >= r.sleeper_exit_ms - 1_000) return 'tool_call_returned_only_when_the_detached_process_exited';
  return 'tool_call_returned_while_the_detached_process_was_running';
}

/** Did codex.exe exit promptly after turn.completed, or only once the detached process had exited (or not at all)? */
function exitVerdictOf(r) {
  if (r.spawn_error) return 'spawn_error';
  if (r.watchdog_killed) return r.turn_completed_ms === null ? 'killed_by_watchdog_before_turn_completed' : 'did_not_exit_killed_by_watchdog';
  if (r.turn_completed_ms === null) return 'exited_without_turn_completed';
  const afterTurn = r.codex_exit_ms - r.turn_completed_ms;
  // The sleeper's exit is polled every 500 ms, so it is seen up to about a second late.
  const withSleeperExit = r.sleeper_exit_ms !== null && r.codex_exit_ms >= r.sleeper_exit_ms - 1_000 && r.codex_exit_ms - r.sleeper_exit_ms <= 5_000;
  if (withSleeperExit && afterTurn > 2_000) return 'exited_only_when_the_detached_process_exited';
  if (afterTurn <= 10_000) return 'exited_promptly_after_turn_completed';
  return 'exited_late_for_another_reason';
}

function verdictOf(r) {
  r.tool_call_verdict = toolCallVerdictOf(r);
  r.exit_verdict = exitVerdictOf(r);
  const started = r.items.find((i) => i.type === 'item.started' && i.command);
  const done = r.items.find((i) => i.type === 'item.completed' && i.command);
  r.command_started_ms = started ? started.at : null;
  r.command_completed_ms = done ? done.at : null;
  r.sleeper_running_at_codex_exit = r.sleeper_pid === null || r.codex_exit_ms === null ? null : (r.sleeper_exit_ms === null || r.sleeper_exit_ms > r.codex_exit_ms + 1_000);
  return `${r.tool_call_verdict}; ${r.exit_verdict}`;
}

async function runVariant(opts, ctx, variant, mcpArgs, log) {
  const stamp = iso().replace(/[:.]/g, '-');
  const work = join(ctx.workRoot, `${variant}-${stamp}`);
  mkdirSync(work, { recursive: true });
  const command = commandFor(variant, opts.childSeconds);
  const prompt = promptFor(command);
  const args = ['exec', '--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox', '--skip-git-repo-check', '--json', '--cd', work, '-c', `model_reasoning_effort="${opts.effort}"`, ...mcpArgs, '-'];
  const r = {
    variant, work, command, args, started_at: iso(), codex_pid: null, spawn_error: null,
    thread_started_ms: null, turn_completed_ms: null, usage: null, items: [], agent_messages: [],
    codex_exit_ms: null, codex_exit_code: null, codex_close_ms: null, stderr_tail: '', nonjson_stdout: [],
    sleeper_pid: null, sleeper_pid_seen_ms: null, sleeper_exit_ms: null, sleeper_cleanup: null,
    diagnostics: [], watchdog_killed: false, watchdog_kill: null, verdict: null,
  };
  const t0 = Date.now();
  const rel = () => Date.now() - t0;
  let child;
  try {
    child = spawn(ctx.codex, args, { cwd: work, env: minimalEnv(), windowsHide: true, shell: false, stdio: ['pipe', 'pipe', 'pipe'] });
  } catch (error) {
    r.spawn_error = String(error);
    r.verdict = verdictOf(r);
    return r;
  }
  r.codex_pid = child.pid ?? null;
  log(`[${variant}] codex pid ${r.codex_pid}, work ${work}`);
  child.once('error', (error) => log(`[${variant}] spawn error: ${String(error)}`));
  let buffer = '';
  const onLine = (line) => {
    let event;
    try { event = JSON.parse(line); } catch { if (r.nonjson_stdout.length < 20) r.nonjson_stdout.push(line.slice(0, 300)); return; }
    const at = rel();
    const item = event.item ?? null;
    if (event.type === 'thread.started') r.thread_started_ms = at;
    if (event.type === 'turn.completed') { r.turn_completed_ms = at; r.usage = event.usage ?? null; log(`[${variant}] turn.completed at +${at} ms`); }
    if (event.type === 'turn.failed' || event.type === 'error') r.items.push({ at, type: event.type, detail: JSON.stringify(event).slice(0, 600) });
    if (item && item.type === 'command_execution') {
      r.items.push({ at, type: event.type, id: item.id ?? null, status: item.status ?? null, exit_code: item.exit_code ?? null, command: String(item.command ?? '').slice(0, 900), output: item.aggregated_output === undefined ? null : String(item.aggregated_output).slice(0, 600) });
    } else if (item && item.type === 'agent_message' && event.type === 'item.completed') {
      r.agent_messages.push({ at, text: String(item.text ?? '').slice(0, 300) });
    } else if (item && event.type === 'item.completed') {
      r.items.push({ at, type: event.type, item_type: item.type ?? null, status: item.status ?? null });
    }
  };
  child.stdout.on('data', (chunk) => {
    buffer += chunk.toString('utf8');
    let index;
    while ((index = buffer.indexOf('\n')) >= 0) { const line = buffer.slice(0, index).trim(); buffer = buffer.slice(index + 1); if (line) onLine(line); }
  });
  child.stderr.on('data', (chunk) => { r.stderr_tail = (r.stderr_tail + chunk.toString('utf8')).slice(-6000); });
  let exited = false;
  child.once('exit', (code) => { exited = true; r.codex_exit_ms = rel(); r.codex_exit_code = code; log(`[${variant}] codex exited (${code}) at +${r.codex_exit_ms} ms`); });
  child.once('error', (error) => { exited = true; r.spawn_error = String(error); r.codex_exit_ms = rel(); });
  child.once('close', () => { r.codex_close_ms = rel(); });
  child.stdin.on('error', () => undefined);
  child.stdin.end(prompt, 'utf8');

  const pidFile = join(work, 'child.pid');
  let snapAt10 = false;
  while (true) {
    await sleep(500);
    const now = rel();
    if (r.sleeper_pid === null && existsSync(pidFile)) {
      const n = Number(readFileSync(pidFile, 'utf8').trim());
      if (Number.isInteger(n) && n > 0) { r.sleeper_pid = n; r.sleeper_pid_seen_ms = now; log(`[${variant}] detached sleeper pid ${n}`); }
    }
    if (r.sleeper_pid !== null && r.sleeper_exit_ms === null && !alive(r.sleeper_pid)) { r.sleeper_exit_ms = now; log(`[${variant}] detached sleeper exited at +${now} ms`); }
    if (exited) {
      // Keep measuring the sleeper until it ends (or should have ended), so the verdict can relate both exits.
      const sleeperDeadline = (r.sleeper_pid_seen_ms ?? now) + (opts.childSeconds + 30) * 1000;
      if (r.sleeper_pid === null || r.sleeper_exit_ms !== null || now > sleeperDeadline) break;
      continue;
    }
    if (r.turn_completed_ms !== null && !snapAt10 && now >= r.turn_completed_ms + 10_000) {
      snapAt10 = true;
      r.diagnostics.push({ at: now, label: 'still running 10 s after turn.completed', codex: procInfo(r.codex_pid), codex_children: childrenOf(r.codex_pid), sleeper: procInfo(r.sleeper_pid) });
      log(`[${variant}] codex still running 10 s after turn.completed; snapshot taken`);
    }
    const overGrace = r.turn_completed_ms !== null && now >= r.turn_completed_ms + opts.graceSeconds * 1000;
    const overCap = r.turn_completed_ms === null && now >= opts.hardCapSeconds * 1000;
    if (overGrace || overCap) {
      r.diagnostics.push({ at: now, label: overGrace ? `still running ${opts.graceSeconds} s after turn.completed: killing` : `no turn.completed after ${opts.hardCapSeconds} s: killing`, codex: procInfo(r.codex_pid), codex_children: childrenOf(r.codex_pid), sleeper: procInfo(r.sleeper_pid) });
      r.watchdog_killed = true;
      r.watchdog_kill = killTree(r.codex_pid);
      log(`[${variant}] watchdog killed codex: ${JSON.stringify(r.watchdog_kill)}`);
      const until = Date.now() + 15_000;
      while (!exited && Date.now() < until) await sleep(250);
      if (!exited) { r.codex_exit_ms = rel(); r.codex_exit_code = null; }
      exited = true;
    }
  }
  if (r.sleeper_pid !== null && r.sleeper_exit_ms === null) { r.sleeper_cleanup = stopSleeper(r.sleeper_pid, opts.childSeconds); log(`[${variant}] sleeper cleanup: ${JSON.stringify(r.sleeper_cleanup)}`); }
  const closeUntil = Date.now() + 5_000;
  while (r.codex_close_ms === null && Date.now() < closeUntil) await sleep(100);
  r.verdict = verdictOf(r);
  r.ended_at = iso();
  log(`[${variant}] verdict ${r.verdict}`);
  return r;
}

async function main() {
  const opts = parseArgs(process.argv.slice(2));
  mkdirSync(opts.out, { recursive: true });
  const logFile = join(opts.out, 'harness.log');
  const log = (line) => appendFileSync(logFile, `${iso()} ${line}\n`);
  const resultsFile = join(opts.out, 'results.json');
  const results = { done: false, started_at: iso(), harness: 'codex-exec-hang-repro.mjs', options: { ...opts }, environment: {}, runs: [], error: null };
  const save = () => writeFileSync(resultsFile, JSON.stringify(results, null, 2));
  save();
  try {
    const found = opts.codex ?? newestCodex();
    const codex = found ? resolve(found) : null;
    if (!codex || !existsSync(codex)) throw new Error(`codex.exe not found (${codex ?? 'no candidate'})`);
    const version = spawnSync(codex, ['--version'], { encoding: 'utf8', windowsHide: true, timeout: 30_000 });
    const workRoot = opts.workRoot ?? join(process.env.LOCALAPPDATA || os.tmpdir(), 'codex-exec-hang-repro');
    mkdirSync(workRoot, { recursive: true });
